## D-001: Language and Runtime

**Decision**: Go {{ .GoVersion }}
**Rationale**: originating project standard for microservices. Strong concurrency, fast compilation, single binary deployment.
**Alternatives considered**: Node.js (available for frontend-adjacent services)

---

## D-002: HTTP Router

**Decision**: `github.com/go-chi/chi/v5`
**Rationale**: Lightweight, idiomatic Go router. Composable middleware. originating project standard.
**Alternatives considered**: gin (heavier), net/http (no middleware composition)

---

## D-003: ORM / Database Access

**Decision**: `github.com/uptrace/bun` with PostgreSQL driver
**Rationale**: Type-safe query builder, good migration support via goose, originating project standard.
**Alternatives considered**: GORM (too magic), raw sql (too verbose), sqlc (extra tooling)

---

## D-004: Database

**Decision**: PostgreSQL 16, shared `internal_main_db`
**Rationale**: originating project standard. All services share the main DB unless isolation needed.
**Migration tool**: goose (SQL files in `migrations/`)

---

